WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.400 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  Nana watt weakest of the Aztec gods  sickly and covered in pimples had been  chosen to form a new world there had  already been four worlds each set in  motion by its own Lord Sun and each in  turn destroyed the first by Jaguars the  next by winds the next by rains of fire  and the force by floods to establish the  fifth son Lord Quetzalcoatl serpent had  gone to the underworld and returned with  the bones of earlier people nourishing  them with his own blood to create new  life but for them to have a world to  live in another God had to leap into the  great bonfire and become the fifth son  the Lord of sustenance and the Lord of  fire had chosen not a wat for this test  while the Lord of rain and the lord of  the four quarters had picked their own  offerings the proud rich Texas Tech hunt  first the chosen ones had to complete a  four day fasting and bloodletting ritual  Nana wand had nothing but cactus thorns  with which to bleed himself and fir  branches to paint with his red offering  but he resolved to try his best  meanwhile Texas TECA he flaunted his  riches using magnificent Jade spines and  branches adorned with iridescent Quetzal  feathers for his own blood offering when  four days had passed the fire was  roaring high four times proud Texas Tech  on approached the flames and four times  he pulled back in fear humble nanawatai  stepped forward the other gods painted  him chalky white include feathers to him  without hesitation he threw himself into  the flames a fire blackened Eagle  swooped over the fire grabbed to nunna  wat and carried him into the sky their  Lord and Lady sustenance bathed him sat  him on a feathered throne and wrapped a  red band around his head inspired by  Nana wat taxis ticket threw himself into  what was left of the fire cooled ashes a  Jaguar jumped over the fire pit but  couldn't carry taxis ticket into the sky  when tech sees tech out reached the  horizon a band of goddesses trust him in  rags still he shined just as brightly as  nanobot but since he had shone far less  bravery and much more pride one of the  gods picked up a rabbit and tossed it in  his face  dimming his life but the fifth world  still wasn't truly established Nana watt  Lord Sun shined for four days straight  without moving through the sky like all  the previous Suns had moved back in  their home teotihuacan the gods began to  worry  they sent obsidian Hawk up to ask what  was wrong the Nahuatl replied that just  as he had sacrificed himself to become  Lord Sun he now needed the nourishing  blood of the other gods in order to move  through the sky enraged at the  suggestion Lord dawn stepped up and shot  an arrow at Lord Sun Lord Sun shot back  and his Quetzal feathered arrow struck  Lord dawn in the face turning him to  frost before anyone else could act  rashly the other gods turned to each  other to discuss what to do of course no  one wanted to sacrifice themselves but  nor did anyone want to act like Lord  dawn  besides Nana watt had held up his end of  the bargain to nourish the earth how  could they refuse to nourish him in  return they remembered how even the  wimpy tech sees TECA had eventually  managed to emulate Nana Watts bravely at  long last five other gods agreed to  sacrifice themselves one by one more  deaths stabbed them in the heart of an  obsidian knife offering their bodies to  their newborn son as the last God made  the sacrifice Lord ket's alcoa blew the  embers of the great fire back to life  and the Sun began to move through the  sky at last assuring in the fifth page  thanks to a pimply weakling whose  fortitude inspired all the other gods  the Sun moves along its daily path the  rabbit faced moon following in its wake  if you enjoyed this myth check out this  playlist for more epic tales  [Music]

